dx - Run Bazel workflows

dx <command> [flags] [scope ...] [-- bazel-options ...]

Scopes: labels, patterns, files, or dirs. No scope means //... for most commands.

Exit codes: 0 success, 2 usage error, 1 failed check.

Usage: dx [COMMAND]

Commands:
  security      run security audit over resolved scopes (non-mutating; live Gitleaks plus advisory/vuln backends)
  license       run license audit over resolved scopes (non-mutating; live license-policy plus SPDX backend)
  lint          run lint analysis over resolved scopes (check by default; --apply writes fixes)
  typecheck     run typecheck analysis over resolved scopes (check by default; --apply writes fixes)
  format        check or rewrite formatting over resolved scopes (check by default; --apply writes fixes)
  generate      emit/sync BUILD files (Gazelle pipeline; check by default; --apply writes generated sources)
  build         run Bazel build over resolved targets
  test          run Bazel test over resolved targets
  coverage      collect LCOV coverage with optional threshold
  run           build and run runnable targets sequentially (explicit labels/patterns; file/dir scopes need exactly one runnable)
  deploy        build and run a single deployable target
  check         run format+lint+typecheck+generate checks in order (non-mutating)
  fix           apply format+lint+typecheck+generate fixes in order (check by default; --apply writes fixes, then verifies with a read-only check)
  clean         prune unselected managed state, never Bazel outputs unless --bazel (check by default; --apply prunes; no scopes)
  update        update dependencies per set through qualified resolvers (check by default; --apply writes updates)
  bump          widen one declared requirement to a new version (check by default; --apply widens)
  migrate       rewrite breaking changes across releases (upgrade-only; check by default; --apply migrates; --dry-run plans without writes)
  codegen       collect codegen outputs with atomic commit (check by default; --apply writes managed state)
  env           collect the managed development environment (check by default; --apply writes managed state)
  setup         collect setup outputs with atomic commit (check by default; --apply writes managed state)
  init          scaffold dx into a foreign tree (absent-only; check by default; --apply scaffolds)
  new           scaffold a minimal qualified project for one language (absent-only; check by default; --apply scaffolds)
  upgrade       one-shot pin+migrate+setup composition with recovery pointer (check by default; --apply upgrades; --dry-run plans without writes)
  hooks         manage Git hooks via hermetic Git (check by default; --apply installs)
  status        report workspace and target status
  version       report version and pin drift
  watch         watch for changes and rebuild (local only)
  owners        query owners of files via Bazel query
  deps          query dependencies of targets
  why           explain why a target depends on another
  completion    emit shell completions from the CLI grammar (bash|zsh|fish|powershell; --check verifies without writing)
  docs          build, check, and serve the mdBook documentation site (non-mutating; --check validates without rendering)
  bazel         forward raw arguments to the Bazel launcher
  capabilities  print machine-readable CLI and workspace capabilities (no downloads; --workspace-capabilities adds workspace facts)
  verify        run one committed verification set from dx.verify.toml in order (non-mutating; stops after the first required failure)
  rerun         rerun the failed test targets recorded in a run-output receipt on the current workspace (never a historical reproduction)
  tests         list configured test targets with optional Rust case enumeration (non-mutating; --cases builds and lists without running bodies)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Environment:
  DX_WORKSPACE=<dir>
      Default for --workspace.
  DX_DRY_RUN=<bool>
      Default for --dry-run.
  DX_QUIET=<bool>
      Default for --quiet.
  DX_VERBOSE=<bool>
      Default for --verbose.
  DX_COLOR=<mode>
      Default for --color.
  DX_OUTPUT=<mode>
      Default for --output.
  DX_FAIL_ON=<level>
      Default for --fail-on.
  <bool> is on for 1|true|yes|y|on and off for 0|false|no|n|off.
      Anything else is a usage error. An empty value is unset.
  RUST_LOG=<filter>
      Override --verbose and --log-level.
  NO_COLOR=<any>
      Disable color output.
  BUILD_WORKSPACE_DIRECTORY=<dir>
      Workspace start under `bazel run`.
  dx.toml (committed) and dx.local.toml (local-only, gitignored) carry the same defaults as the DX_ variables, below the environment.
      Local beats committed. In CI the local file and DX_ variables are ignored; flags still win.
      A legacy .dx/config.toml with a new file present is a usage error naming both files.
      An unknown key is a usage error.
